;; confidence-range-low — a claim's confidence must be >= 0.0 (the lower arm of
;; the [0.0, 1.0] range; REQ-KG-003 / REQ-KG-012).
;;
;; Booklogic port of the sh:minInclusive 0.0 arm of the tbf:confidence range
;; constraint in assets/shapes.ttl:
;;   sh:path tbf:confidence ; sh:minInclusive 0.0 ; sh:maxInclusive 1.0 .
;;
;; The compiler has no OR/disjunction within one rule, so the range is two
;; constraints: confidence-range.edn covers sh:maxInclusive (conf > 1.0) and
;; this one covers sh:minInclusive (conf < 0.0). Both carry the SAME authored
;; :message and the SAME :path ("#confidence") so the rdflib path's
;; message-remap (keyed on the SHACL path) stays unambiguous — a confidence
;; violation maps to the single range message regardless of which arm fired.
;; This closes C-1: pyshacl enforces BOTH bounds, and now the Cozo path does too,
;; so a confidence < 0.0 claim is non-conforming under BOTH engines.
;;
;; The literal 0.0 stays UNQUOTED so it compares against the typed Float column;
;; the compiler guards the comparison with !is_null so a null-confidence claim is
;; dropped (its missing-value concern belongs to the minCount shape, not range).
(defconstraint :confidence-range-low
  :message "Claim confidence must be in [0.0, 1.0]."
  :path "https://example.org/book-knowledge#confidence"
  :where [[?c :claim/id ?focus]
          [?c :claim/confidence ?conf]]
  :filter [[< ?conf 0.0]])
